{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(arcsec({x}^{2})).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-19082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formulae for the derivatives of $arctan$ and $arcsec$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arctanx) & =\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx) & =\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formulae above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(arcsec({x}^{2}))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(arcsec({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(arcsec({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}|\\sqrt{({x}^{2})^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+(arcsec({x}^{2}))^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}|\\sqrt{({x}^{2})^{2}-1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{arcsec}^{2}({x}^{2}))}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-19082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "309884a6f71b3b85c064bbc5460c7a3891cbec32e76d8b8f3bdc8fa325ab048b"} {"question" "q-19082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-19082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{arcsec}^{2}({x}^{2}))}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}(1+{arcsec}^{2}({x}^{2}))}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+arcsec({x}^{2}))}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}(1-arcsec({x}^{2}))}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{arcsec}^{2}({x}^{2}))}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-19082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}(1+{arcsec}^{2}({x}^{2}))}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-31951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=2arcsec(6x-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-31951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formula for the derivative of $arcsec$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2arcsec(6x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec(6x-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{(6x-1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x-1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{{(6x-1)}^{2}-1}}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{36{x}^{2}-12x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{4(9{x}^{2}-3x)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-31951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "309884a6f71b3b85c064bbc5460c7a3891cbec32e76d8b8f3bdc8fa325ab048b"} {"question" "q-31951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-31951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-x}}"] ["math" "-\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{3{x}^{2}-x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-31951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6}{|6x-1|\\sqrt{9{x}^{2}-3x}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}\\cdot arccot\\,(\\sqrt{x}).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{arccot(\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}\\cdot arccot(\\sqrt{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})\\cdot arccot(\\sqrt{x})+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,(\\sqrt{x})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\cdot arccot(\\sqrt{x})+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{1+{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})] \\\\  & =\\frac{arccot(\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{1+x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{arccot(\\sqrt{x})}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2(1+x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "309884a6f71b3b85c064bbc5460c7a3891cbec32e76d8b8f3bdc8fa325ab048b"} {"question" "q-341145" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341145" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2(1+x)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot arccot\\,x.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{arccot\\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The formula for the derivative of $arccot$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot arccot\\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x)\\cdot arccot\\,x+{log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccot\\,x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\cdot arccot\\,x+{log}_{4}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{arccot\\,x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡x}{1+{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "309884a6f71b3b85c064bbc5460c7a3891cbec32e76d8b8f3bdc8fa325ab048b"} {"question" "q-341147" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341147" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\ln(x)}{\\ln(4)(1+x^2)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=\\frac{{3}^{x}}{arccsc\\,x}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\frac{1}{arccsc\\,x}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{1}{|x|{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, we let $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)=arccsc\\,x,$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)\\cdot arccsc\\,x-{3}^{x}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})}{{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}. \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\frac{arccsc\\,x}{{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}+\\frac{{3}^{x}}{{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\frac{1}{arccsc\\,x}+\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\frac{1}{|x|{(arccsc\\,x)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "309884a6f71b3b85c064bbc5460c7a3891cbec32e76d8b8f3bdc8fa325ab048b"} {"question" "q-341179" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341179" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3^x\\ln(3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341179" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"} {"question" "q-341179" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3^x}{\\sqrt{x^2-1}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005730/state.json" "file_sha256" "c65689cc3c9135754bf09107f8594fafc59b481b8b0824cc3d209aa1560f43d2"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1107 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
